essary  that something happens but i'm positive  that there will be a movement and a  positive change over the next days  i have a question and yeah this  yes um i think it is important now to  implement the regime on the external  border  i told you and you said it too that we  have an intensive discussion about the  internal border measures that are  hampering not only the single market and  our economy but also difficult for the  labor market for example  with those who are commuters and  we have published the guidelines the  guidelines got a lot of  backing so i think the first step will  be that we ease  the tension in those regions where  internal borders have been borrow  measurements have been put up  in general so that they are more  flexible and they  are more targeted on  leaving leaving the leaving the way  to the flow of goods and those people  who have to cross the border urgently  but i think it will take quite a while  still till  we reach the lifting of the internal  border it was an intensive discussion  i think it was uh it was clear at the  end of the discussion  that we have to be very careful with our  single market  and this is the most economic economy  in the economy it's the most precious  instrument we do have so it's of ut most  importance  that we keep it going and keep it up  because  it is of essential importance  mainly being in such a crisis as we are  right now  president  videos have a question from the new york  times as well from martina stevies  president of the council and of the  president to the president of the  commission can you clarify which  countries  agree to go ahead with the broader  issues measures  namely was it to 27 minus ireland plus  non-eu  schengen  i take that one um so  we got a lot of approval of  member states actually it was  uh none of them who  up uh was negative on this proposal  but we know that at the moment being the  uk  is not planning on  implementing external border  restrictions  as far as i understand today they advise  their people uh not to travel abroad  this is as far as i got from the news uh  the state of play in the uk at the  moment being  and of course this goes then for island  too because we have a  common travel zone important is  that the uk citizens are eu citizens so  i think  we still have to repeat that because we  are in the transition  uh phases so for for the uk citizens and  of course northern ireland things stay  as they are  i have one last question from a lot of  news outlets  [Music]  in europe  [Music]  thank you very much  so  [Music]  you

